codex
I found the container-specific cause: processes get namespace-local PIDs that are absent from the mounted `/proc`, while Lean 4.22 resolves its executable via `/proc/<getpid()>/exe`. `/proc/self/exe` is still valid. I’m applying a narrowly scoped audit helper that redirects only that exact self-executable lookup to `/proc/self/exe`, then rerunning the unchanged trusted preflight with the pinned Lake/Lean binaries. This is an environment repair, not a modification of any proof or generated source.
